  "Attributes": [
    {
      "Id": 759987,
      "attributeType": "LongString",
      "attributeName": "AIDescription",
      "attributeRelationType": "None",
      "Value": "## 18 Years Clarence: A Commodore 64 Chronicle\n\nStep back into the chilling world of Oceania, eighteen years after the events of *1984*. *18 Years Clarence* for Commodore 64 plunges you into the life of Clarence, a young man raised entirely within the Party's oppressive regime. Clarence, unlike many, possesses a flicker of independent thought, a dangerous anomaly in a society built on absolute conformity.\n\nThe game blends exploration, puzzle-solving, and stealth elements as you navigate the decaying remnants of London and uncover a clandestine network of rebels attempting to restore individuality.  Your actions directly impact the narrative; choices made regarding interactions with Party officials and fellow citizens will shape Clarence’s fate and the rebellion’s success. \n\nGameplay revolves around avoiding the ever-watchful eyes of the Thought Police, deciphering coded messages, and gathering vital information.  Utilize limited resources – food, medicine, and safe houses – to survive.  The game features a haunting soundtrack and pixel art that perfectly captures the bleak atmosphere of Orwell’s dystopian vision, offering a unique and challenging experience for Commodore 64 enthusiasts."
    },
